uced to  it as a 16 8 and actually i had realized  that i met several people who did fast  in this way basically what that means is  they ate for eight hours throughout the  day and they stopped eating for six  hours and i realized that i didn't want  to begin that fast because for me that  was a drastic change i had never done  something like that before if i got  hungry at 12 in the morning i ate at 12  in the morning and so i wanted to focus  on building the habit instead of just  focusing on the numbers so initially for  me i started 12 12 and then i progressed  two more hours and then i finally  progressed to 16. however i noticed that  a lot of people what they do is they  skip breakfast and then that's how they  fast basically maybe something like 12  noon to 8 p.m but for me lattes are my  thing y'all like that gets me out of the  bed like yes latte time for me having  the ability to eat breakfast is very  motivating to get me out of the bed  early in the morning five-ish and so i  wanted to do something that i would  stick with rather than what everybody  else was doing and that's one thing that  i would recommend to you is if you do  want to do intermittent fasting whether  it's prolonged or shortened do something  that works for you that you will stick  with not just because this is the right  way to do it and another reason that i  personally prefer to skip dinner over  breakfast is because i find that this  helps me be more productive and make  better use of my time because the time  that i would have spent cooking  something prepping it eating it cleaning  up those dishes all that time is time  that i can spend cleaning up my house  and tidying up so that the day later  that next morning i can actually get up  and work on productive things instead of  procrastinating because there's a pile  of dishes and i  i need to clean the pile of dishes  instead of working out you know because  let's be honest sometimes we  procrastinate with productive things  th