  people people actually did tell me these  things actually that if people give you  food you must clear your plate because  it's showing gratitude that they are  giving you their resources their  lifeline and growing a poor that is  literally they're giving you of their  life resources so you can eat and so if  you leave your plate halfway you're not  grateful for that and so i grew up  believing that that if you're given food  you must finish your meal  and also i guess i had this feeling of  if i like something i must eat it eat it  eat it because i don't know if i'm gonna  have that thing again um and this was  more of when i was a child because when  i grew up here in the united states we  had plenty of food that was never an  issue but i know that when i was a child  i could recognize that other children  had foods that i didn't have having  certain foods was a once in a few months  kind of a thing and so when i would go  to visit other people and they'd have  cereal it was like oh my gosh cereal i  could tease you it has a toy in the box  it was phenomenal and i  at that point i think is when i began to  just eat the moment i had the ability to  eat something that was not with not  normally in my home and i remember that  this is a child i never actually told my  grandma but i have a feeling she knows  when i would visit my grandma's house  and she had hot dogs which were not  something that we particularly had in  our home i would actually hide and i  actually would eat the whole pack of the  hot dogs and uh never explain who it was  i'm sure she knew who it was but so  these were the types of habits that i  had hoarding food eating it right away  here recently my husband actually  pointed out you know you eat slower and  when he said that it was like this light  bulb came out and i said you're right i  actually savor my food now and i also  noticed that one of the things that has  changed is that i now have the ability  to kind of stop where i love this  particular meal but you know what i'm  satiated i'm okay and i think it  specifically came out because sometimes  i experienced  bloating  immediately after or just this feeling  of fullness and nausea if i ate too much  after having a long fast so that's one  thing is i had to start eating slowly  and leaner meals so that i wouldn't  experience those side effects and so  having done that routinely and  repetitively i didn't realize this has  changed in me i'm embarrassed to admit  that but i think that a lot of people  can resonate with that especially if  you've had emotional struggles with  eating where you just eat when you're  anxious because that can happen you know  when you're sad and this really helped  me also in a way that it helped me make  better choices of the foods that i was  eating because if i only have this  certain time to eat  or if i'm doing this hard work of not  eating for this extended period of time  i didn't just do all this work for  nothing it's kind of the way that i  thought about it and so it has helped me  make better choices of the way that i  eat and having a healthier relationship  with food and then also helping remove  that guilt because you know what it's  okay if i do have some cake and not to  really feel guilt and attack myself for  the things that i am eating but rather  just overall make healthier choices to  nourish my body so also another thing  that i really liked is that when i'm  fasting i don't feel bloated i just feel  good i have more energy i just i feel  light in a way it's odd to explain i  have more time to really do other things  and focus my productive energy on other  things and actually contrary to what  many might believe working out when  you're in a fasted state is really good  for you it can help you actually build  muscle rather than lose muscle so just  overall it felt really good too fast  after i kind of learned that i didn't  have to torture myself and also just  really paying attention to my hydrati